      "technical_explanation": "The flagged line is inside a test file (file_role: test) and constructs a fixture object whose image field is set to an inline base64 data URI placeholder representing a multimodal image attachment. The scanner's shady-link heuristic matched URL-like literal content in the string, but the literal is a self-contained data URI with no external host, no network scheme implying remote access, and no reachable runtime network behavior. The fixture is consumed only by the test's assertions, which verify that the injection runtime preserves image attachments and other extensions' prompt blocks when inserting category text into outgoing message arrays. Elsewhere in the same test, request handling is exercised against a locally defined fetch stub that records request bodies for assertion; no outbound connection is made. No credentials, exfiltration path, persistence, or obfuscation are involved, and the capability exercised matches the extension's stated purpose of injecting content into SillyTavern generation requests.",
